{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Ra'ukha yakhilu</b> (You were seen, they trembled) — from the sound of the thunder." "<b>Zeram mayim avar</b> (A flood of waters passed) — over them, over the mountains." "<b>Natan tehom kolo</b> (The deep gave its voice) — the roar of the sea and the river." "<b>And the meaning of rom</b> (height) — the reverse of tehom (deep), as in: 'For I lift up my hand to the heavens' (Deuteronomy 32:40) — by way of [the reverse]."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {3 "The Hebrew breaks off mid-thought after 'דרך' (way/path); the argument appears incomplete or possibly corrupt. Rendered hyper-literally; the verse cited is Deut. 32:40, where God lifts His hand to heaven, exemplifying 'rom' as the opposite of tehom."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:57.010549933Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}